sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant Client as Customer Channel
    participant Agent as Agent API / Orchestrator
    participant Session as Trusted Session Context
    participant Security as Security / Verification
    participant Banking as Banking API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Audit as Audit Logging

    Customer->>Client: Start conversation / ask question
    Client->>Agent: Send request with session credentials
    Agent->>Session: Load conversation state
    Agent->>Security: Resolve trusted identity and verification state
    Security-->>Agent: Identity context / verification status
    Note over Agent,Security: Support-session verification establishes identity for permitted support actions; it does not establish, change, or upgrade the customer's regulatory KYC tier.

    alt Identity required but not verified
        Agent-->>Client: Request appropriate verification
        Client-->>Customer: Present verification prompt
    else Request can proceed
        Agent->>Agent: Classify intent and choose read or write path
        Note over Agent,Banking: For KYC questions, use RAG for general policy requirements. For a customer's actual KYC tier/status or restrictions, use only an authorized account lookup and report recorded values; tier changes or reviews follow a separate approved process.

        alt Read-only banking query
            Agent->>Banking: Request operation using trusted session context
            Banking->>Security: Enforce ownership and permission checks
            Security-->>Banking: Allow or deny
            alt Allowed
                Banking->>DB: Read authorized records
                DB-->>Banking: Records
                Banking->>Audit: Record tool/action outcome
                Banking-->>Agent: Result
                Agent-->>Client: Answer using returned result
            else Denied
                Banking->>Audit: Record denial
                Banking-->>Agent: Authorization error
                Agent-->>Client: Safe refusal / next step
            end
        else Sensitive write or consequential action
            Agent->>Banking: Prepare action with trusted identity and idempotency key
            Banking->>Security: Enforce identity, permission and step-up requirements
            Security-->>Banking: Allow or deny preparation
            alt Preparation allowed
                Banking->>DB: Persist pending action, expiry and audit record
                DB-->>Banking: Pending action reference
                Banking-->>Agent: Confirmation summary and reference
                Agent-->>Client: Ask customer to confirm exact action
                Client-->>Customer: Display confirmation details
                Customer->>Client: Confirm or cancel
                Client->>Agent: Submit confirmation response
                Agent->>Banking: Submit pending-action reference and approval signal
                Banking->>DB: Validate expiry, action match, single-use status and ownership
                DB-->>Banking: Validation result
                alt Approval valid
                    Banking->>DB: Atomically claim approval and execute authorized state change
                    DB-->>Banking: Execution outcome
                    Banking->>Audit: Record final outcome
                    Banking-->>Agent: Confirmed success or known failure
                    Agent-->>Client: Report outcome
                else Expired, mismatched, reused or invalid
                    Banking->>Audit: Record rejected confirmation
                    Banking-->>Agent: Confirmation rejected
                    Agent-->>Client: Explain that confirmation is invalid: restart if appropriate
                end
            else Preparation denied
                Banking->>Audit: Record denied preparation
                Banking-->>Agent: Authorization / verification error
                Agent-->>Client: Safe refusal or verification next step
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Agent,DB: The agent coordinates the conversation. The Banking API and PostgreSQL remain authoritative for pending confirmations and banking writes.
